for name,title in [('cpu','Processor-side layer transition'),('memory','Memory-side escape')]:
 folder=ROOT/f'data/em-latest-ddr-d8-{name}';case=json.load(open(folder/'case-input.json'));r=json.load(open(folder/'normalized-report.json'));mesh=json.load(open(folder/'mesh-summary.json'));conv=json.load(open(folder/'convergence.json'));path=f'/em/latest/{name}/';out=ROOT/'public'/path.strip('/');out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
 cards=''.join(f'<article class="card"><h3>{layer} · {"GND plane" if layer.startswith("inner") else "outer signal layer + exported GND copper"}</h3><a href="{path}{layer}.png"><img src="{path}{layer}.png" alt="{title}: {layer} ground return-current heatmap" loading="lazy"></a><a href="{path}{layer}.png">Open full-resolution image</a></article>' for layer in ['top','inner1','inner2','bottom'])
 processor_images='<h2>Processor escape · inner-plane voids</h2><p>Actual PCB geometry around U1, with DDR_D13 highlighted. These are PCB inspection images, without an EM heatmap.</p><div class="grid">'+''.join(f'<article class="card"><h3>{layer} · U1 escape and GND voids</h3><a href="/em/latest/processor/{layer}.png"><img src="/em/latest/processor/{layer}.png" alt="U1 processor BGA escape, {layer} ground voids"></a></article>' for layer in ['inner1','inner2'])+'</div>' if name=='cpu' else ''
 cpu_note='The CPU signal via is now near (−1, −18) mm. This local crop isolates its top-to-bottom transition; the processor package lies outside it. The input fixture joins the cut top trace to inner1 GND.'
 memory_note='The input fixture joins the actual memory signal pad to its nearest exported package GND pad. It is a test fixture; package internals and the real driver are omitted.'
 html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>AM3352 · DDR return-current EM</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/em/latest/style.css"></head><body data-case="{name}"><header><h1>DDR_D8 return current · latest PCB</h1><p>{('Processor escape · 400 MHz / 1 GHz / 4 GHz' if name=='cpu' else 'Memory escape · 400 MHz')} · top/bottom signals · inner1/inner2 GND planes</p><nav><a class="pill {'active' if name=='cpu' else ''}" href="/">Processor BGA escape</a><a class="pill {'active' if name=='memory' else ''}" href="/em/latest/memory/">Memory-side escape</a><a class="pill" href="https://tscircuit.com/astra/am3352-sbc#pcb">Source PCB</a></nav></header><main><h2>{title}</h2><p>{cpu_note if name=='cpu' else memory_note} The cut bottom trace is terminated through a 50 Ω fixture to inner2 GND.</p><div class="notice"><strong>New-board solves completed; accuracy is provisional.</strong> Only selected connection/region combinations have solved fields; other connections are PCB inspection only. These local crops truncate plane coupling and exclude GND connections outside the crop. Element-order checking does not establish local-density, crop or fixture convergence. No validated “bad loop” verdict is available.</div><div id="stats" class="stats"></div><div class="controls"><label for="connection">Connection</label><select id="connection" aria-label="Connection"></select><label for="frequency">Frequency</label><select id="frequency"><option value="400mhz">400 MHz</option><option value="1ghz">1 GHz</option><option value="4ghz">4 GHz</option></select><label for="layer">GND / return layer</label><select id="layer"><option value="inner1">Inner1 · GND</option><option value="inner2">Inner2 · GND</option><option value="top">Top</option><option value="bottom">Bottom</option></select><button id="processor-escape">U1 escape overview</button><button id="fit">Fit EM area</button><button id="downstream-em">DDR_D8 downstream</button><button id="fit-connection">Full connection</button><button id="processor-pad">Signal &amp; GND pads</button><button id="memory-pad">Memory pad</button><button id="fit-board">Full PCB</button><button id="plus">Zoom +</button><button id="minus">Zoom −</button><label><input type="checkbox" id="show-heat" checked> EM heatmap</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="flow" checked> Phase 0° arrows</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="show-ground" checked> Highlight GND net &amp; return terminal</label><label>PCB visibility <input id="pcb-opacity" type="range" min="0.1" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.65"></label><label>Heat opacity <input id="heat-opacity" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.6"></label><button id="download-view">Download this view</button></div><p id="source-note" hidden></p><div id="stage" class="stage"></div><div class="legend"><div><div class="bar"></div><div class="scale"><span>0.01</span><span>0.1</span><span>1</span><span>10</span><span>100 A/m</span></div></div><span style="color:#087d8c">● Cyan: selected connection</span><span style="color:#ae279c">Magenta: GND pads / vias and selected source return</span><span>GND via current: hover over a via for mA</span></div><p id="layer-note"></p><p>Choose from 47 DDR connections. DDR_D8 and DDR_D13 have U1 processor EM overlays. DDR_D8 also has downstream and memory-side runs; other connections are PCB inspection only. Use PCB visibility and heat opacity to compare copper and return current.</p><p>Drag to pan; scroll to zoom. Labels stay the same size. Colors show surface-current phasor magnitude |K|. White arrows show instantaneous direction at phase 0°, which changes through the RF cycle.</p><details><summary>Locate this trace and both experiments on the PCB</summary><p>Cyan: full selected DDR_D8 route. Amber: the two local EM domains.</p><a href="/em/latest/board-overview.svg"><img style="width:100%;max-height:550px" src="/em/latest/board-overview.svg" alt="Latest PCB with DDR_D8 highlighted and EM regions marked"></a></details>{processor_images}<section id="live-results" hidden></section><section id="em-results"><h2>All four layer images</h2><div class="grid">{cards}</div><h2>Simulation parameters and checks</h2><p>{conv['summary']}</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Solver</th><td>Palace v0.14.0 · 3D frequency-domain FEM Maxwell · order {r['finite_element_order']}</td></tr><tr><th>Excitation</th><td>400 MHz · 1 V signal-to-GND normalized peak phasor · 50 Ω input reference and load</td></tr><tr><th>Stackup assumption</th><td>Top 1.6 / inner1 1.4 / inner2 0.2 / bottom 0 mm from bottom. Internal dielectric thicknesses are not supplied by the PCB export.</td></tr><tr><th>Materials</th><td>FR4 εr 4.3, tanδ 0.02 · copper 5.8×10⁷ S/m · copper foil 35 µm · via plating 25 µm</td></tr><tr><th>Mesh</th><td>{mesh['nodes']:,} nodes · {mesh['elements']:,} tetrahedra · 0.1 mm minimum target · octagonal barrels</td></tr><tr><th>Domain</th><td>x [{case['bounds_mm'][0]}, {case['bounds_mm'][2]}], y [{case['bounds_mm'][1]}, {case['bounds_mm'][3]}] mm · 5 mm air padding · first-order absorbing boundary</td></tr><tr><th>Geometry</th><td>{len(case['signal_vias'])} selected signal via; {len(case['ground_vias'])} GND vias. Exported GND vias span top→inner1; signal vias span top↔bottom. The model follows those spans. Any inner1↔inner2 GND stitching through fabrication barrels, plated holes or copper outside these crops is omitted. This can strongly affect impedance; fabrication spans/stubs require confirmation. Other signal/power copper, package internals and decoupling are omitted.</td></tr><tr><th>Displayed ground faces</th><td>Inner1 upper face (toward top signal); inner2 lower face (toward bottom signal); outer GND faces. These are face currents, not sums across the two faces of a plane.</td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Results, source snapshot and reproduction files</summary><p><a href="{path}report.json">SI phasor report</a> · <a href="{path}palace.json">Solver configuration</a> · <a href="{path}convergence.json">Element-order comparison</a> · <a href="{path}via-currents.json">Via currents</a> · <a href="https://github.com/tscircuit/return-current-trace-demo">Source repository</a></p><p>PCB SHA-256: <code>{r['board_snapshot_sha256']}</code></p></details></section><footer>Earlier-board results: <a href="/em/">historical EM pilot</a> · <a href="/approximation.html">historical frequency-independent approximation</a>. These use a different PCB snapshot.</footer></main><script src="/em/latest/pcb-view.js?v=actual-u1-pads-v1"></script></body></html>'''
 (out/'index.html').write_text(html)
 if name=='cpu':(ROOT/'public/index.html').write_text(html)
